# Level two

Let a level-two page take people straight to a task, with an order you can defend. People arriving here should not meet another vague category. For example, an installation topic can list guides in reading order, while a reference list is alphabetical so people can find a known item. The hierarchy itself is described in [Mainstream browse](../mainstream-browse.html).

## When to use it

Use it for a focused set of guides, device instructions or settings explanations. Add a short description where two destinations sound alike.

## Structure and behaviour

Give the page a specific subtopic title and a route to its parent. Choose reading order for a procedure and alphabetical order for known-item lookup. When a list mixes a guide, a native page and an external document, make each destination type clear.

## Home Assistant boundary

The example subtopics are documentation structures, not installed Home Assistant routes. Avoid hidden accordions on a short list. Changing the browse order does not change device priority or automation behaviour.

